  "description": "*What kind of ‘filter’ do we use when we speak?*\n\nGoh Dam, a timid college student who always hid her true feelings, collapses on the street one day and disappears. A year later, she reappears. She reveals she has contracted a rare disease called ‘Rayleigh Syndrome’... What? A disease where your true feelings burst out? Through words that both wound and comfort, she navigates her unfiltered, tumultuous youth.\n\n(Source: Naver, translated)",
